### Justification

The claim is false on multiple levels: [Lead Stories](https://www.google.com/search?q=Did+the+Breitbart+News+report+that+the+daughter+of+Delaware+Democratic+Senator+Chris+Coons+and+seven+other+underaged+girls+were+featured+on+Hunter+Biden%27s+laptop%3F&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8) explicitly confirmed in a fact-check headlined "Fact Check: Breitbart Did NOT Report Daughter Of Sen. Coons And 7 Underaged Girls Were 'Featured' On Hunter Biden's Laptop" that Breitbart News never published such an article, and [PolitiFact](https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/oct/20/facebook-posts/fact-checking-unproven-claims-about-hunter-biden-a/) stated there is "no evidence that a computer hard drive previously belonging to Hunter Biden contains illicit images of Coons' teenage daughter," rating related claims as "False." While Chris Coons is indeed a Democratic U.S. Senator from Delaware with a daughter named Maggie, no independent forensic experts, law enforcement agencies, or legal proceedings have verified the presence of underage content on the laptop, and the computer repair shop owner himself told reporters he did not see child pornography on the device. The claim fabricates both the source (a nonexistent Breitbart report) and the underlying allegation, and is therefore refuted.